  "verbalization": "Longistyline C appears to have multiple targets that ultimately converge on Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Longistyline C may act through a series of intermediate molecules, including Sucrase-isomaltase, Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, and Peripheral myelin protein 22, which are all targets of other compounds. These intermediaries may serve as bridges in a broader biological pathway, potentially involving cellular processes such as protein degradation or metabolic regulation. The presence of multiple distinct targets pointing to the same final destination implies that Longistyline C could exert its effects through different mechanisms, possibly by modulating the activity of these intermediaries. While the exact mechanism by which Longistyline C influences Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2 remains unclear, the integrated evidence suggests a possible role in regulating cellular functions through a cascade of molecular interactions.",
